Stack: Python @@python@@, `uv` for dependencies, `ruff` for lint and format, `mypy` for types, `pytest` for tests, Make for commands.

## Working rules

- Read `README.md` first for setup and the command list.
- Match the shape of an existing module and its test before inventing a new pattern. `@@example_path@@` is the reference until real code exists.
- Prefer small, focused changes. Do not bundle unrelated refactors into a feature or fix.
- Do not invent new Make targets or scripts when an existing one covers the workflow.

## Commands

- Install: `make install` (uv sync and pre-commit hooks)
- Lint: `make lint` (ruff check and format check) and `make lint-yaml` (yamllint)
- Type check: `make typecheck` (mypy, strict)
- Format: `make format`
- Test: `make unit-tests` or `make unit-tests path=<dir>`
- Full list: `make help`

